    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d544">

                <pb facs="0590" n="490" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg490"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/6109: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Morris</hi>)<anchor n="32" xml:id="d544-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-01-09T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 9,
                                1920—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>7. Repeat following to Legation Peking, to Harris and to Consul Vladivostok to be
                    given by him to Smith, Stevens, and Graves. It will be released to press at
                    Washington Tuesday January 13th.<anchor n="33" xml:id="d544-f2"/></p>
                <pb facs="0591" n="491" xml:id="pg491"/>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“On December 8, 1919, the Japanese Ambassador at Washington, pursuant to
                        instructions from his Government, invited the attention of the Secretary of
                            State<anchor n="34" xml:id="d544-f3"/> to the recent unfavorable
                        development of the situation in Siberia, and inquired whether the United
                        States proposed to maintain the <hi rendition="#italic">status quo</hi>, or
                        to proceed to entire or partial withdrawal of its troops, or whether it was
                        ready to send reenforcements in case of need.</p>
                    <p>“The Secretary of State has today communicated to the Japanese Ambassador the
                        decision of the Government of the United States in the following
                        memorandum:</p>
                    <p>[Here follows memorandum printed on <ref target="#pg487">page 487</ref>.]</p>
                </quote>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d544-f1" n="32" type="source" xml:id="d544-f1-content">
                <p>The same, except the first sentence, to the Ambassador in Great Britain as no.
                    19, with instructions to “Communicate following to Foreign Office and repeat to
                    Paris, Rome and Prague for similar action.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d544-f2" n="33" xml:id="d544-f2-content">
                <p>The memorandum was released to the press Jan. 16.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d544-f3" n="34" xml:id="d544-f3-content">
                <p>Memorandum not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
